  m_text: "The Northern Plains lie to the south of the Himalayas, extending from
    Punjab in the west to Assam in the east. Formed by the Indus, Ganga, and Brahmaputra
    river systems, these plains cover about 7 lakh sq. km and are one of the most
    densely populated and agriculturally productive regions of the world.\t"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
