  m_text: <b>Northern plains of India or Indo-Gangetic plains </b>form the second
    largest physiological division of India with an approximate area of 21 percent
    of the total geographic area of India. The Ganga, Indus and Brahmaputra flow
    through these plains and provide plenty of water for irrigation. Hence it is,
    agriculturally, the most fertile land in India and forms the backbone of economy
    of rural India.
